{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DyvjoJES4z93xHffQgJv9L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Quality estimation framing完全成立，correlation-selection gap被视为novel conceptual contribution，paper写作和positioning达到Main标准\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Quality estimation (AUROC/ρ for selective prediction) 被接受为first-class contribution，不要求selection improvement\"\n      - \"Correlation-selection gap被认为是novel finding而非negative result的包装\"\n      - \"2×2 matrix (Qwen×LLaMA × SciERC×CoNLL) + 3-seed robustness被认为generalization充分\"\n      - \"与Nédellec & Xia 2026成功区分：SJ解决其自承的surface matching limitation\"\n      - \"RE full ρ弱 (~0.21-0.30) 被接受为task-complexity boundary的supporting evidence而非weakness\"\n      - \"Paper presentation达标：≥3 figures + 35+ refs + 清晰信号分类法 + 对concurrent work的显式对比\"\n    number_ranges:\n      reviewer_overall_arr: [3.5, 4.0]\n      acceptance_prob_main: [0.40, 0.60]\n      acceptance_prob_findings: [0.75, 0.90]\n      perceived_novelty: [3.5, 4.0]\n      perceived_soundness: [3.5, 4.5]\n      n_major_weaknesses_per_review: [0, 1]\n      rebuttal_addressable_pct: [0.85, 1.0]\n      # 以下为reviewer关注的empirical metrics（数据固定，但reviewer聚焦点不同）\n      focal_auroc_gap_structural_vs_logprob: [0.10, 0.17]  # reviewer看NER best config (voting 0.73 vs logprob 0.56)\n      focal_rho_gap: [0.15, 0.36]  # NER ρ gap: voting 0.50 vs logprob 0.14\n      cross_config_ner_structural_gt_logprob_rate: [1.0, 1.0]  # 6/6 NER configs，全部structural>logprob\n      effective_claim_count_accepted: [3, 3]  # 三条claim全部land\n    narrative_direction: \"原始3-claim framing完全成立。Claim 1以voting AUROC 0.73 vs logprob 0.56为headline，SJ作为generalizable complement。Claim 2 (correlation-selection gap) 定位为paper最具practical insight的发现——改变practitioners对structured TTS的认知。Claim 3提供explanatory depth。Claims无需调整强度。\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Quality estimation被接受但novelty受质疑（'expected for structured outputs'），gap finding有趣但practical impact不清晰，scope concerns不致命但需softening\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"至少1位reviewer质疑novelty：structural metrics适用于structured outputs被视为intuitive\"\n      - \"Correlation-selection gap被视为interesting observation但非standalone contribution\"\n      - \"Reviewer要求≥3 datasets或larger model (70B) 以增强generalization，但接受当前scope作为initial study\"\n      - \"Nédellec & Xia 2026被引用为overlapping work，partial novelty reduction\"\n      - \"RE full ρ_sj < 0.30被视为limiting claim scope，但conditional analysis (ρ=0.37-0.41) 部分挽回\"\n      - \"NER selection failure (all ≤ greedy) 被至少1位reviewer视为significant limitation而非contribution\"\n      - \"Paper presentation adequate但不exceptional\"\n    number_ranges:\n      reviewer_overall_arr: [3.0, 3.5]\n      acceptance_prob_main: [0.12, 0.30]\n      acceptance_prob_findings: [0.45, 0.65]\n      perceived_novelty: [2.5, 3.5]\n      perceived_soundness: [3.0, 4.0]\n      n_major_weaknesses_per_review: [1, 2]\n      rebuttal_addressable_pct: [0.50, 0.80]\n      focal_auroc_gap_structural_vs_logprob: [0.05, 0.10]  # reviewer聚焦weaker configs或RE (SJ 0.58 vs logprob 0.64，SJ输)\n      focal_rho_gap: [0.05, 0.15]  # reviewer看RE full或averaged across tasks\n      cross_config_ner_structural_gt_logprob_rate: [0.80, 1.0]  # reviewer可能include RE full where SJ loses\n      effective_claim_count_accepted: [2, 2]  # Claim 1 accepted (weakened), Claim 2 downgraded to observation, Claim 3 questioned\n    narrative_direction: \"Claim 1 从'novel signals'调整为'systematic empirical comparison'——贡献在taxonomy而非individual signal。Claim 2 需补充concrete practical guidance（decision flowchart：何时用voting/SJ/logprob）以回应'so what'。Claim 3 从'diagnostic framework'弱化为'empirical analysis'。增加applicability讨论：closed-source API场景（无logprob）中structural signals的独特价值。Target Findings。\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"被视为negative result paper且novelty不足；concurrent work被认为scooping；selection failure和RE weakness主导reviewer讨论\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Reviewer将paper定性为'self-consistency doesn't work for IE'——negative result缺乏sufficient depth\"\n      - \"Nédellec & Xia 2026被视为doing the same study，structural metrics被视为minor extension over surface matching\"\n      - \"Correlation-selection gap被dismiss为'obvious: instance-level ≠ sample-level is well-known in calibration literature'\"\n      - \"2 NER + 1 RE dataset + only 8B models被视为fatally narrow scope\"\n      - \"WNUT abandoned (>50% F1=0, structural rho not significant) 被发现或推断，进一步削弱generalization\"\n      - \"Reviewer期待selection improvement或novel method，pure comparison被视为insufficient venue contribution\"\n      - \"NER best-of-N全部≤greedy被解读为the method fundamentally doesn't work\"\n    number_ranges:\n      reviewer_overall_arr: [2.5, 3.0]\n      acceptance_prob_main: [0.02, 0.08]\n      acceptance_prob_findings: [0.15, 0.35]\n      perceived_novelty: [1.5, 2.5]\n      perceived_soundness: [2.5, 3.5]\n      n_major_weaknesses_per_review: [2, 4]\n      rebuttal_addressable_pct: [0.20, 0.45]\n      focal_auroc_gap_structural_vs_logprob: [0.00, 0.05]  # reviewer聚焦RE full (SJ < logprob) 和WNUT (structural fails)\n      focal_rho_gap: [-0.04, 0.05]  # reviewer引用RE full SJ 0.21 vs logprob 0.25 (SJ输)\n      cross_config_ner_structural_gt_logprob_rate: [0.60, 0.80]  # reviewer扩展scope至RE+WNUT，win rate降低\n      effective_claim_count_accepted: [0, 1]  # 仅Claim 1的NER部分勉强accepted\n    narrative_direction: \"需要完全reframe。新angle：'Why Self-Consistency Fails for Structured Prediction: An Analysis of the Correlation-Selection Gap'。以gap作为PRIMARY contribution（而非第三条claim），转型为TTS scaling文献中的cautionary/analytical paper。论证：(1) TTS scaling laws隐含假设confidence与selection ability aligned，structured prediction违反此假设；(2) 用quality estimation数据解释gap的mechanism（instance-level aggregation destroys per-sample ranking info）；(3) 提出formal conditions under which consistency-based selection should/shouldn't work。Lead with negative finding + explanation，positive quality estimation data降为supporting evidence。同一venue (EMNLP)，不同paper archetype：从'signal comparison + positive finding'转为'surprising negative + theoretical explanation'。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40197,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40197},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61abbce1-f972-4103-93ea-bdd9365daee2","uuid":"275ff6e5-e87e-4f57-b0d1-2a7c5c028ea1"}
